Third-party datasets redistributed in this repository
=====================================================

This repository redistributes the annotation files of two public benchmark datasets so that the results reported in the PlotPick paper can be reproduced exactly. For ChartX this is every record of both splits (6000 entries: the 1152-entry test split with all its fields, and the 4848-entry validation split reduced to the image name, chart type, title and CSV table the benchmark reads); for PlotQA it is a 1000-entry subset of the test split. No chart images are redistributed; they are fetched from the original sources by pipeline/fetch_chartx_images.py.

Licence texts are in LICENSES/.

ChartX
------
Files: external/chartx/chartx_test.json, external/chartx/chartx_val.json
Copyright: the ChartX authors (Shanghai AI Laboratory and collaborators)
Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/InternScience/ChartX
Licence: Apache-2.0 as stated on the Hugging Face dataset card; the GitHub repository of ChartX carries CC-BY-4.0.
Citation: Xia et al., "ChartX & ChartVLM: A Versatile Benchmark and Foundation Model for Complicated Chart Reasoning", arXiv:2402.12185.

The copies here are MODIFIED. Ground-truth errors were found during evaluation in eight test-split figures (CSV columns not shown in the chart, errors in the redrawing code, and stacked-bar annotations giving totals instead of segment values). In chartx_test.json the CSV tables of three of them (bar_num_363, line_num_315, line_num_361) were corrected by removing the column the chart does not show; the other five are unchanged here (three had their images regenerated, and images are not stored in this repository; two were only reported upstream). The changes are listed in external/chartx/CORRECTIONS.md so that the modifications are identifiable, as Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires.

PlotQA
------
Files: external/plotqa_test_1000.json, external/plotqa_test_100.json
Source: https://github.com/NiteshMethani/PlotQA
Licence: CC-BY-4.0 (dataset), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Citation: Methani, Ganguly, Khapra and Kumar, "PlotQA: Reasoning over Scientific Plots", WACV 2020.
These files are a subset of the PlotQA test split, adapted into the field layout this benchmark reads: the first 1000 (and the first 100) entries of the test split in the order of the conversion published at https://huggingface.co/datasets/achang/plot_qa, each reduced to the first series of its chart, with the serialised annotation cut to 500 characters. They are provided without warranties, as CC-BY-4.0 section 5 sets out.

Not redistributed
-----------------
Subsets of ChartQA, ChartQAPro and ChartMuseum were used in exploratory work that is not reported in the paper. They are not included here because their redistribution terms were not established. The scripts that reference them remain, and will not run until that data is obtained from the original sources.

PubMed Central content
----------------------
results/pmc/, reports/, pairs.json, candidates.csv and excluded_pairs.json contain values and metadata from figures and tables in PubMed Central Open Access Subset articles, identified by PMCID. Each source article carries its own licence; consult the article record before reusing its content. No patient-identifiable data is included; all values are aggregate figures as published.

Derived values
--------------
The result files under results/ and the summaries under reports/ embed ground-truth values copied from ChartX and PlotQA, so the terms above apply to them as well.
